Receive Diun update webhooks

POST /api/hooks/diun stores image updates Diun reports. It needs no session
but requires "Authorization: Bearer <PIHUB_WEBHOOK_TOKEN>", compared in
constant time; 404 when no token is set, 401 for a wrong one, 415 for
non-JSON, 400 for a malformed body, else 200 {"stored": bool}. It works in
read-only mode, since receiving alerts edits nothing.

PIHUB_WEBHOOK_TOKEN accepts env:/file: references and must resolve to at
least 32 characters, or pi-hub exits with code 2: a long random token is
what keeps the unthrottled hook unguessable. Updates are saved to
updates.json next to the config (PIHUB_UPDATES overrides), and /api/state
now always carries an "updates" list matched to the services.

JSON body parsing moved into one helper shared by every POST endpoint;
existing endpoints answer exactly as before. Reviewed by an independent
verifier (approved).

